<title>HUNGARY: Two dead, 23 injured as buses collide in Hungary.</title>
<headline>Two dead, 23 injured as buses collide in Hungary.</headline>
<dateline>DEBRECEN, Hungary 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>An Italian-registered coach collided with a Romanian bus on a highway in eastern Hungary on Wednesday, killing two people and injuring 23.</p>
<p>&quot;What we know so far is that an Italian-licensed bus ... tried to pass a parked ambulance car, when it collided head-on with a Romanian-licensed bus,&quot; lieutenant colonel Sandor Marton, the officer in charge of the Hajdu-Bihar county policy, told Reuters over the phone.</p>
<p>The collision happened in thick fog, he said, adding that police have no information yet on the severity of the injuries.</p>
